bringup.c and bringup.h are original darwin-lab code. The T8103 apcie port-0
bring-up sequence they follow (step order, register offsets, bit meanings, poll
targets and timeouts, the ADT local-tunable record layout, the link-speed rule
and the PMGR power-state fields) is taken from m1n1:

  sources/m1n1-baseline (commit 121fcbf35d4501814b58ca5347926a4173b6a512)
    src/pcie.c      sha256 fc285646b6c1bdb950b792d55326caf838b58d57799e9ad1327e5ec4d38f86df
    src/pmgr.c      sha256 dad4bebb125aab3811f2674654c20641956f945f2cbd496ac6d99d6df73299e3
    src/tunables.c  sha256 5c63846309fdc055c9e6306b597852b8a44ca61ba4fad4f7098876814cefee43

The only data copied as-is is the 11-entry T8103 fuse transfer table
(pcie_fuse_bits_t8103 in src/pcie.c), reproduced in bringup.c as fuses_t8103.
No m1n1 functions are copied. No Linux (GPL pcie-apple.c or otherwise) or Apple
source, kext or firmware is used. m1n1's licence follows.

